\name{cellucid_history_step}
\alias{cellucid_history_step}
\title{Read a step}
\usage{
cellucid_history_step(viewer, step, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{step}{A step, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{at}, \code{bookmark}, \code{branch}, \code{by} (Who acted), \code{children}, \code{code}, \code{group}, \code{id}, \code{kind}, \code{label}, \code{merged} (Changes merged into it (a drag, a gesture)), \code{ms} (How long its action took), \code{notes}, \code{params} (Its parameters as the details show them (cells as counts)), \code{parent}, \code{reads} (The inputs its result depends on), \code{reason}, \code{replay_of}, \code{shown} (On the path to the step shown now), \code{squashed}, \code{stale}, \code{status}, \code{touches}, \code{tracker}, \code{type}, \code{until}, \code{v}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
One step in full: its parameters, pseudocode, who took it and when, what it changed and read, its notes and bookmark, and why it is stale.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.step} (History). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_step(viewer, step = "s3")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
